{"crc":"c225c81a","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at the bug report, the issue is that `Line3D` object has no attribute `_verts3d`. This happens when a `Line3D` object gets into an invalid state where `_verts3d` is missing.\n\nThe problem occurs in `art3d.py` in the `Line3D.draw()` method, which tries to access `self._verts3d` without checking if it exists. This can happen if the line data was set with incompatible dimensions (like passing a numpy array instead of a scalar), which causes an error during `set_data_3d` or `set_3d_properties`, leaving `_verts3d` unset.\n\nLet me check the `Line3D` class and its `draw` method to add proper error handling:\n\n```python\n# path: lib/mpl_toolkits/mplot3d/art3d.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    @artist.allow_rasterization\n    def draw(self, renderer):\n        xs3d, ys3d, zs3d = self._verts3d\n        xs, ys, zs = proj3d.proj_transform(xs3d, ys3d, zs3d, self.axes.M)\n        self.set_data(xs, ys)\n        super().draw(renderer)\n        self.stale = False\n=======\n    @artist.allow_rasterization\n    def draw(self, renderer):\n        if not hasattr(self, '_verts3d'):\n            return\n        xs3d, ys3d, zs3d = self._verts3d\n        xs, ys, zs = proj3d.proj_transform(xs3d, ys3d, zs3d, self.axes.M)\n        self.set_data(xs, ys)\n        super().draw(renderer)\n        self.stale = False\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZT1JZY340XDMACAVCB7RNQP","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZT1JZXX9N8AQDYVF9Q4DARH"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786506743.9064589}
{"crc":"b1bbe553","kind":"substrate.TriggerFired","payload":{"factory":"validator","firing_key":null,"input_sha256":"sha256:87517ccdbd8893134184690a42054cdc27976e1df8ce55f9d6cd587cde5cfcd2","instance":"01KZT1K432ZM51T91Z9CAWDDE0","resolved_input":{"response":"Looking at the bug report, the issue is that `Line3D` object has no attribute `_verts3d`. This happens when a `Line3D` object gets into an invalid state where `_verts3d` is missing.\n\nThe problem occurs in `art3d.py` in the `Line3D.draw()` method, which tries to access `self._verts3d` without checking if it exists. This can happen if the line data was set with incompatible dimensions (like passing a numpy array instead of a scalar), which causes an error during `set_data_3d` or `set_3d_properties`, leaving `_verts3d` unset.\n\nLet me check the `Line3D` class and its `draw` method to add proper error handling:\n\n```python\n# path: lib/mpl_toolkits/mplot3d/art3d.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    @artist.allow_rasterization\n    def draw(self, renderer):\n        xs3d, ys3d, zs3d = self._verts3d\n        xs, ys, zs = proj3d.proj_transform(xs3d, ys3d, zs3d, self.axes.M)\n        self.set_data(xs, ys)\n        super().draw(renderer)\n        self.stale = False\n=======\n    @artist.allow_rasterization\n    def draw(self, renderer):\n        if not hasattr(self, '_verts3d'):\n            return\n        xs3d, ys3d, zs3d = self._verts3d\n        xs, ys, zs = proj3d.proj_transform(xs3d, ys3d, zs3d, self.axes.M)\n        self.set_data(xs, ys)\n        super().draw(renderer)\n        self.stale = False\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```","round":1,"slot":0},"trigger_id":"validate"},"producer":null,"schema":"substrate.TriggerFired@1","seq":15,"t":1786506743.9065862}
